            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-mark"></span> THE SHORT, PLAIN-LANGUAGE GUIDE</p>
            <h1>Use TenderLens in <em>five simple steps.</em></h1>
            <p class="guide-lede">You can explore the sample without an account. The examples are made up. Live search is available only when the optional service is running.</p>
            <a class="button button-dark" href="index.html#demo">Open the sample report <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
          <aside class="guide-note"><span class="guide-note-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span><p><strong>First time here?</strong><br>Start with the sample. It shows how a tender rule can be checked and where the source appears.</p></aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 / GET STARTED</p>
          <h2 id="steps-title">Five things to try</h2>
          <div class="guide-step-grid">
            <article class="guide-step-card"><span>1</span><h3>Open a sample report</h3><p>Choose a requirement to see its sample status and the document that it came from.</p><a href="index.html#demo">Go to the report <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
            <article class="guide-step-card"><span>2</span><h3>Explore tender examples</h3><p>Search the made-up examples, filter by type, or open a card for a short review checklist.</p><a href="index.html#opportunities">Go to sample tenders <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
            <article class="guide-step-card"><span>3</span><h3>Check the document order</h3><p>Pick a file in the order panel to see how a later update might change an earlier rule.</p><a href="index.html#precedence">Go to document order <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
            <article class="guide-step-card"><span>4</span><h3>Save your bidder profile</h3><p>Save a local draft or sign in to sync basic organization details across devices. This does not check eligibility.</p><a href="index.html#profile">Go to bidder profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
            <article class="guide-step-card"><span>5</span><h3>Build a strategy preview</h3><p>Enter values to make a draft checklist, clarification prompts and EMD cash scenario. Always verify the original tender.</p><a href="strategy.html">Open strategy tools <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section guide-section-muted" id="strategy-tools" aria-labelledby="strategy-guide-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">02 / STRATEGY PREVIEW</p>
            <h2 id="strategy-guide-title">What the new tools do</h2>
            <p class="guide-copy">The preview uses tender and bidder values that you enter. It does not read tender files, save the submitted form, or make a legal or eligibility decision.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-setup">
            <ol>
              <li>Use clarification prompts to identify questions you may want to ask through the official tender channel.</li>
              <li>Review possible capability gaps. TenderLens does not list or verify consortium partners.</li>
              <li>Download the checklist as a CSV draft; entered values are not supporting evidence.</li>
              <li>Use the EMD figure as a cash scenario only. The tool does not confirm exemptions or permitted instruments.</li>
              <li>If you choose public-source search, the tender title and portal are sent to the configured search provider. Search results need manual verification.</li>
            </ol>
            <a class="guide-api-link" href="strategy.html">Open the strategy preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section guide-section-muted" aria-labelledby="status-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">03 / READ THE RESULTS</p>
            <h2 id="status-title">What do the labels mean?</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-status-list">
            <article><span class="guide-status status-met">MEETS</span><p>The sample profile has the evidence needed for this example rule.</p></article>
            <article><span class="guide-status status-missing">MISSING</span><p>The sample profile does not show the requested evidence.</p></article>
            <article><span class="guide-status status-review">REVIEW</span><p>The wording or evidence needs a person to check the original file.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="words-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">04 / USEFUL WORDS</p>
            <h2 id="words-title">A short glossary</h2>
            <p class="guide-copy">Tender documents use a lot of abbreviations. Here are the ones used on this site.</p>
          </div>
          <dl class="guide-glossary">
            <div><dt>Tender</dt><dd>A buyer’s request for companies to offer goods, work or services.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>ATC</dt><dd>“Additional Terms and Conditions”: extra rules added by the buyer.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Corrigendum</dt><dd>An official notice that changes or clarifies an earlier tender.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Clause</dt><dd>One numbered rule or paragraph inside a tender file.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>A document or record that helps show whether a requirement is met.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Bidder profile</dt><dd>Basic details about the business preparing a bid. Save a local draft or sync it to your signed-in account.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section guide-section-muted" id="live-search" aria-labelledby="live-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">05 / OPTIONAL LIVE SEARCH</p>
            <h2 id="live-title">Turn on current tender search</h2>
            <p class="guide-copy">This needs the TenderLens backend and a TinyFish API key. The key stays on the server; never put it in the website code.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-setup">
            <ol>
              <li>Install <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">uv</a> and sync the project dependencies.</li>
              <li>Copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code>, then add your TinyFish key to <code>TINYFISH_API_KEY</code>.</li>
              <li>Start the API with <code>uv run uvicorn backend.main:app --reload</code>.</li>
              <li>In another terminal, run <code>python -m http.server 4177</code> and open <code>http://localhost:4177</code>.</li>
              <li>Open “Search current tender notices” and submit a phrase. Only that phrase and the selected portal are sent.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="guide-copy"><strong>Other backend features:</strong> <code>GEMINI_API_KEY</code> turns on clause/conflict analysis, while <code>TAVILY_API_KEY</code> enables the backup web search. Both are optional for the website and account pages; the model setting defaults to <code>gemini-3.8-flash</code>.</p>
            <p class="guide-warning"><strong>What is connected?</strong> Live search uses the backend, and the separate Strategy tools page builds a preview from values you enter. Tender fetching and source-document scorecard review are not connected to a webpage form.</p>
            <a class="guide-api-link" href="http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the local API reference <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="account-setup" aria-labelledby="account-setup-title">
        <div class="container guide-two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">06 / ACCOUNTS AND SAVED TENDERS</p>
            <h2 id="account-setup-title">Set up sign-in once</h2>
            <p class="guide-copy">TenderLens uses Supabase Auth and Supabase Postgres for accounts. FastAPI provides the public project settings and continues to run live tender search. User rows are protected with database policies.</p>
            <div class="guide-final-links"><a class="button button-dark" href="signup.html">Create an account <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="signin.html">Already have an account? Sign in</a></div>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-setup account-setup-card">
            <ol>
              <li>Create a Supabase project. Copy its Project URL and <strong>publishable key</strong> from the Connect dialog into <code>SUPABASE_URL</code> and <code>SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY</code> in your private <code>.env</code>. The publishable key is designed to be exposed to the browser; never use a secret or service-role key here.</li>
              <li>Run <code>supabase/setup.sql</code> once in Supabase Dashboard → SQL Editor. It creates the bidder-profile and saved-tender tables and locks rows to their account with row-level security.</li>
              <li>In Supabase Authentication, enable Email and Google. For Google, create a Google OAuth client, copy its client ID and secret into the Supabase Google provider settings, and add the callback URL shown by Supabase to Google Cloud.</li>
              <li>Add <code>http://127.0.0.1:4177/**</code> and <code>http://localhost:4177/**</code> under Supabase Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs. Set the site URL to the address you use locally.</li>
              <li>For email confirmation and password reset in production, configure a trusted SMTP provider in Supabase. The built-in test mailer is intended for limited development use.</li>
              <li>Restart FastAPI with <code>uv run uvicorn backend.main:app --reload</code> and serve the pages at <code>http://127.0.0.1:4177</code>. Sign in, update your profile, then test saving a link from a live search result.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="guide-warning"><strong>Keep secrets out of chat and GitHub.</strong> Google OAuth client secrets and SMTP credentials belong in the Supabase Dashboard. TenderLens only needs the Supabase URL and browser-safe publishable key in the private local environment file. Do not send us keys in chat.</p>
            <p class="guide-copy"><strong>Not needed for this connection:</strong> a direct database password or Supabase secret key. The browser uses Supabase Auth and Postgres Data API with row-level security; FastAPI does not bypass those policies.</p>
            <a class="guide-api-link" href="https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/social-sign-in/auth-google" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supabase Google setup guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section">
        <div class="container guide-final-card">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">PLEASE READ BEFORE BIDDING</p><h2>Always check the original tender.</h2><p>TenderLens is a prototype and cannot promise that a bid will qualify. Ask the buyer when a rule is unclear.</p></div>
